{
  "id": "ep048",
  "duration": 47.831,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.005,
      "text": "Our entire galaxy is sliding toward a central gravitational focal point.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "LaniakeaBoundaries.jpg",
        "credit": "R. Brent Tully (U. Hawaii) et al., SDvision, DP, CEA/Saclay",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LaniakeaBoundaries.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.005,
      "end": 10.775,
      "text": "For years, astronomers only mapped our cosmic neighbors using light-based positions.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SDSS2020.png",
        "credit": "Sloan Digital Sky Survey",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SDSS2020.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.0,
          "end": 10.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.775,
      "end": 17.07,
      "text": "In September 2014, researcher R. Brent Tully tracked how these galaxies actually move.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Shadia-party- R, BRENT TULLY.png",
        "credit": "KimxOnnn",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shadia-party-_R,_BRENT_TULLY.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.767,
          "end": 17.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.07,
      "end": 24.015,
      "text": "Using the Green Bank Telescope, his team mapped a structure spanning 400 to 500 million light-years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Radio telescope at the National Radio Astronomy Observatory in Green Bank, West Virginia LCCN2015634500.tif",
        "credit": "Carol M. Highsmith",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Radio_telescope_at_the_National_Radio_Astronomy_Observatory_in_Green_Bank,_West_Virginia_LCCN2015634500.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.067,
          "end": 21.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 24.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.015,
      "end": 29.385,
      "text": "They named it Laniakea, a Hawaiian word meaning immense heaven or open skies.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.0,
          "end": 29.4,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 29.385,
      "end": 37.38,
      "text": "This supercluster contains approximately 100,000 galaxies, matching the mass of 100 quadrillion Suns.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Map of voids in the CosmicFlows-3 volume of the Local Universe.jpg",
        "credit": "H. M. Courtois, R. van de Weygaert, M. Aubert, D. Pomar\u00e8de, D. Guinet, J. Dom\u00ednguez-G\u00f3mez, E. Florido, L. Galbany, R. Garc\u00eda-Benito, J. M. van der Hulst, K. Kreckel, R. E. Miura, I. P\u00e9rez, S. Planelle",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_voids_in_the_CosmicFlows-3_volume_of_the_Local_Universe.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 37.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.38,
      "end": 43.28,
      "text": "Like water flowing down a valley, all these galaxies are sliding toward the Great Attractor.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "View towards the Great Attractor (eso9954c).tiff",
        "credit": "ESO",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_towards_the_Great_Attractor_(eso9954c).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.367,
          "end": 40.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 40.333,
          "end": 43.267,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.28,
      "end": 47.481,
      "text": "On the outskirts, our own Milky Way remains locked in this giant flow.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "LaniakeaBoundaries.jpg",
        "credit": "R. Brent Tully (U. Hawaii) et al., SDvision, DP, CEA/Saclay",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LaniakeaBoundaries.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.267,
          "end": 47.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
